# width: 120
# The launcher dock and the BOTTOM PANEL are different surfaces and
# they coexist: the launcher dock is the outermost row, and the panel
# sits inside it, as the editor does.
#
# At 120x40 with no launcher dock the panel is rows 26–37 with its
# header (and its `×`) on row 26 — `bottom_dock_toggle.test` pins that.
# The dock's row comes off the EDITOR AREA (`ui.dock.placement =
# .inner`, the default), so the panel inside it shifts up one: the
# panel's header row is 25, and that is where its `×` answers a click.
# The statusline and the `:` line do not move under `.inner`; under
# `.outer` they move up one instead and the panel lands on the same
# rows either way.
write a.txt "one\ntwo\nthree\n"
open a.txt
ex dock always
command view.toggle_bottom_panel
expect screen contains "DIAGNOSTICS"
expect screen contains "New terminal"
# Row 26 is the panel's body now, not its header: clicking there closes
# nothing.
click 117 26
expect screen contains "DIAGNOSTICS"
# Row 25 is the header, and its `×` closes the panel — the dock stays.
click 117 25
expect screen lacks "DIAGNOSTICS"
expect screen contains "New terminal"
